<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Genpei War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1180–1185</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Genpei War was a civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> between the Taira and Minamoto clans from 1180 to 1185. It ended with the destruction of the Taira at the naval Battle of Dan-no-ura in 1185. The victor, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a>, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>, beginning nearly seven centuries of warrior government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/genpei-war.jpg" alt="Genpei War" width="320" height="133" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Motonobu Denkinobu (伝狩野元信) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Genpei_kassen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
